  "definition": "Aromatase is an enzyme that changes certain androgens into estrogens by aromatizing part of the steroid ring and removing the 19-methyl group. It is a membrane-bound enzyme found in estrogen-producing tissues including the ovaries, placenta, testes, adipose tissue, and brain.",
